Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-07-2000||01:23 AM||||  Here's the deal; I am embarking on a two year restoration project of my 85GT. I have given myself ample time to complete my project and hopefully it won't take quite that long. But just in case. I will be driving this car during the cosmetic period, but plan on buying yet another GT to take it's place during the performance period. This is where(unless you are Fred Flintstone) it will be garaged. Here is where I need your help. I am planning some performance upgrades. However, not so many that is not a practical driver. Nor do I plan<BR>on taking it down to Las Vegas Motor Speedway To turn quarter times. I want better than stock but well short of the track. I already have planned on upgraded exhaust(I'm watching your posts)and doing some porting and polishing, highpressure fule pump and oil pump,and ECM upgrades(if available). Now, to the meat of things. A friend of mine suggested boring and strocking the engine. What I would like to know is; has anyone done this type of mod? What is the best(practicle)approach? What about pistons, lifters, lifter springs, head work, ect... Now keep in mind, at this point I an only planning the engine rebuild and I want to keep it CALM! Nothing to raddical. Also, I've bee hearing alot about the Getrag <BR>5 speed; is it a worth while change from  the auto or not. Any help from the myriad experts here is greatly appriciated. <P>  I owned an 84 four banger, in 84. Wasn't to thrilled with it. Had always wanted the 2M6 and finaly got one in 97. Was getting  rather frustrated wit it untill I found This Forum. I have used so much advise from you all; it's like having my own Fiero Shop working just for me, and for that there can<BR>never be enough thanks. Like I always say to those who know morw than I; Your advise and ability are greatly appriciated.<P>  Thanks BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||03-07-2000||01:44 AM||||Here's my suggestions. First I'd go with roller rockers and have the heads worked. Next I would upgrade the ignition system MSD is suppose to be better than the Accel. I have the Accel and it works fine. Next comes the block. If you want more power I would suggest a 3.1L kit. All it does is change your crankshaft and piston rods. Basically it changes your stroke. If you go 1 size over for the bore it becomes a 3.2L. Or you could get yourself a 3.1L or a 3.4L long block and swap everything over. Porting the exhaust manifolds is the easiest and least expensive. Sprint manifold or headers are around $500 (or more). As for the tranny since it's auto right now a shift kit is easiest. To convert to a Getreg you need lots of money! All the hydralic lines and cylinders (master and slave) need to be installed, new console, Shifter and all cables, brackets, Flywheel and New Axles, Man vs auto axles are different lengths. It is much easier to swap 4spd to 5spd than auto to manual. These are about the most you can do without going exotic (3.8L or V-8)<BR>And as usual money plays a factor.<BR>Good Luck!<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||03-07-2000||01:58 AM||||A stroked 2.8 is a 3.1 and boring it to the max makes it a 3.2 engine.  There is no substitute for cubic inches but that last .1 liters does not leave much room for rebuilding later.<BR>The 3.1 is basicly (very) just crank and pistons.  The longer throw on the crank gives more torque from more leverage.  Balance the engine and install a MILD performance cam.  Fuel and spark, intake and exhaust, this will pull longer and harder than stock by a margin that can be felt AND will last as well or better than the stock 2.8 engine.<BR>Common sense and careful building, it'll be fast.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||03-07-2000||08:34 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>   I haven't done anything to the motor of my car just up grading the ignition, intake, exhaust and replaced Valves and valve stem seals. I've attained 15hp over what the factory spec were and I have 96k miles on my current motor.  (blue line) With just this I'm running 14.7 in the 1/4. 3.2 would be nice but reather pricey. TRW pistons, stock rods and crank send them to FFWD (Fast Forward Inc.) they have a process that is better than nitriding making your stock parts nearly bulletproof! If you have the funds and the know how, swapping the Tranny out of an 84 would help a lot too droping your final drive to 4:10, greatly increasing your 0-60 times but don't try to do any top speed records cause she'll fall on her face above 120.  ||||reg||1
